WEBVTT

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:01.670
I wish you to return.

00:00:02.220 --> 00:00:03.020
You'll forget me!

00:00:03.470 --> 00:00:03.850
Never.

00:00:05.830 --> 00:00:06.270
Faith!

00:00:07.390 --> 00:00:08.490
I thought you were dead!

00:00:09.010 --> 00:00:10.530
There's nothing for you here, boy.

00:00:10.850 --> 00:00:13.610
An extraordinary hero returns to Masterpiece.

00:00:13.830 --> 00:00:14.530
Captain Bulldog.

00:00:15.160 --> 00:00:16.640
Suppose I wish to open a mine.

00:00:17.060 --> 00:00:18.960
I'd suppose you'd take the leave of your senses.

00:00:19.750 --> 00:00:20.370
What's your name?

00:00:20.790 --> 00:00:21.690
Demelda Karn.

00:00:21.970 --> 00:00:23.750
Are the rumors true, do you think?

00:00:24.150 --> 00:00:25.810
Society will never forgive him.

00:00:25.970 --> 00:00:26.570
Who is that name?

00:00:26.950 --> 00:00:27.650
Ross Bulldog.

00:00:54.250 --> 00:00:57.550
Hey, what's the steak?

00:01:07.020 --> 00:01:10.050
Gambling again, Poldark. Remind me why you enlisted.

00:01:10.610 --> 00:01:12.070
To escape the gallows, sir.

00:01:13.760 --> 00:01:14.300
Your crime?

00:01:15.140 --> 00:01:19.130
Brawling, sir. Pre-trading. Assaulting a customs official.

00:01:23.530 --> 00:01:25.110
Wastrels and thieves, the lot of you.

00:01:25.880 --> 00:01:29.620
But you'll soon have the honor of redeeming yourselves in the service of king and country.

00:01:31.530 --> 00:01:33.070
You doubt the justice of our cause, sir?

00:01:33.220 --> 00:01:34.780
And what cause would that be, sir?

00:01:36.270 --> 00:01:37.310
Liberty or tyranny?

00:01:37.450 --> 00:01:57.740
I want to leave here, die here, on your feet!

00:02:11.220 --> 00:02:11.760
Wrecking.

00:02:13.930 --> 00:02:14.870
I wish you to return.

00:02:17.030 --> 00:02:17.850
It won't be for long.

00:02:18.440 --> 00:02:18.640
Again.

00:02:20.300 --> 00:02:20.480
Never.

00:03:30.280 --> 00:03:31.300
Better if he had been.

00:03:31.900 --> 00:03:33.740
He's brought little credit to his family.

00:03:35.760 --> 00:03:37.060
His father was no different.

00:03:37.580 --> 00:03:38.580
A scoundrel.

00:03:39.110 --> 00:03:40.270
And a libertine.

00:03:47.140 --> 00:03:49.140
Still, the family name counts for something.

00:03:49.470 --> 00:03:50.890
And now he's to inherit.

00:03:58.970 --> 00:03:59.970
Is my father...

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:02.890
Oh, sir, bless me.

00:04:03.480 --> 00:04:05.720
We had no idea you were awake.

00:04:06.020 --> 00:04:07.150
When did he die?

00:04:09.260 --> 00:04:11.090
Some six months passed.

00:04:12.460 --> 00:04:13.660
You'd had no word.

00:04:15.380 --> 00:04:16.280
None that reached me.

00:04:25.670 --> 00:04:27.030
You're not going home to Nampara?

00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:28.880
To my Uncle Charles first, ma'am.

00:04:30.800 --> 00:04:32.900
Since my father will evidently not be at home,

00:04:33.040 --> 00:04:34.340
I must look for a welcome elsewhere.

00:05:22.360 --> 00:05:24.700
the honours, Verity, and no half-measures.

00:05:25.370 --> 00:05:27.790
I couldn't eat another morsel.

00:05:28.070 --> 00:05:28.890
Beautiful girl.

00:05:29.120 --> 00:05:29.980
You're as thin as a r-

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:31.870
We must fatten you up.

00:05:32.110 --> 00:05:34.430
Perhaps Francis will be able to coax her.

00:05:34.710 --> 00:05:37.690
I happen to like her just as she is.

00:05:39.510 --> 00:05:40.070
Is that the door?

00:05:40.290 --> 00:05:41.690
Were you expecting someone, my dear?

00:05:41.810 --> 00:05:44.870
She's too valuable here to be thinking of gentlemen callers.

00:05:45.390 --> 00:05:50.600
I hope I'm not intruding.

00:05:59.050 --> 00:05:59.830
Get me, boy.

00:06:00.160 --> 00:06:00.920
You survived.

00:06:01.290 --> 00:06:02.730
To see you again, cousin.

00:06:03.540 --> 00:06:04.880
But we had quite despair.

00:06:05.570 --> 00:06:06.350
Hadn't we, Elizabeth?

00:06:07.150 --> 00:06:07.530
Yes.

00:06:09.040 --> 00:06:13.090
Elizabeth, I had no idea you'd be here.

00:06:14.010 --> 00:06:16.750
Do tell us, Ross, how we managed to lose the war.

00:06:16.990 --> 00:06:18.790
By choosing the wrong side, man.

00:06:21.790 --> 00:06:23.150
Wouldn't have wished for a better homecoming.

00:06:23.440 --> 00:06:24.700
I must speak with you, Ross.

00:06:24.920 --> 00:06:26.260
Yes, of course.

00:06:29.460 --> 00:06:29.980
And what...

00:06:30.380 --> 00:06:32.320
What will you do with yourself now, nephew?

00:06:32.950 --> 00:06:35.750
You'll find Dampara not as you left it.

00:06:36.050 --> 00:06:37.110
Damn me, boy.

00:06:37.530 --> 00:06:40.530
We hadn't thought you'd gone to join the blessed above.

00:06:40.710 --> 00:06:43.820
Great aunt, I'm glad to see you are still of the blessed

00:06:43.820 --> 00:06:44.160
below.

00:06:45.860 --> 00:06:47.360
We'd had no word from you.

00:06:47.560 --> 00:06:49.700
So sit here, or else you must be exhausted.

00:06:50.340 --> 00:06:53.330
Elizabeth, catch me my rat.

00:06:58.540 --> 00:06:59.100
Yes, my mom.

00:07:14.490 --> 00:07:18.290
I seem to have interrupted a party. Is this in honor of the peace or the next war?

00:07:19.080 --> 00:07:24.390
No, um, occasion is...

00:07:25.210 --> 00:07:29.070
Something far more pleasant. My boy is to be married.

00:07:30.990 --> 00:07:33.880
That's tremendous. Who is it to be?

00:07:35.550 --> 00:07:36.010
Elizabeth.

00:07:48.450 --> 00:07:53.690
Truly, we're delighted that our two ancient and distinguished families will be united.

00:08:07.770 --> 00:08:09.010
Did my father suffer much, Uncle?

00:08:09.400 --> 00:08:12.190
Ah, a pitiful end.

00:08:13.160 --> 00:08:14.340
Affairs in tatters.

00:08:15.480 --> 00:08:17.900
Next to nothing left for you to inherit.

00:08:18.230 --> 00:08:20.830
Not that we thought you'd be bad to claim it.

00:08:21.940 --> 00:08:24.040
It's a poor Cornwall you've returned to.

00:08:24.580 --> 00:08:27.120
Taxes sky-high, wages in the gutter.

00:08:27.280 --> 00:08:28.960
Mine closures every other week.

00:08:29.080 --> 00:08:29.820
Bad as you, lad!

00:08:30.060 --> 00:08:32.110
Scarred for life, on its knees.

00:08:32.290 --> 00:08:33.070
I can't stay.

00:08:35.050 --> 00:08:37.430
I've only called to let you know I've returned.

00:08:40.520 --> 00:08:42.080
Must rub you for a horse, Charles.

00:08:44.780 --> 00:08:45.580
First a toast.

00:08:52.040 --> 00:08:56.660
Mr. Francis is together.

00:10:12.640 --> 00:10:12.980
John?

00:10:14.040 --> 00:10:14.480
Prudy?

00:10:50.000 --> 00:10:50.200
Mm-hmm.

00:11:01.150 --> 00:11:26.490
On your feet now Judas mr. Roth back from the grave father's personal servant

00:11:26.490 --> 00:11:29.570
You were left in a position of trust

00:11:30.560 --> 00:11:34.660
What could us do, left alone with no master to guide us?

00:11:34.920 --> 00:11:37.060
I'll guide you with the side of my foot in future.

00:11:37.300 --> 00:11:39.270
But see, t'was rumoured he were dead.

00:11:40.180 --> 00:11:41.400
Perhaps you started the tale.

00:11:41.870 --> 00:11:43.650
Ain't no court to accuse us, Mr. Ross.

00:11:43.830 --> 00:11:46.090
T'n right, t'n fair, t'n fit, t'n friendly.

00:11:46.900 --> 00:11:50.340
You'll get friendly if I don't see my face reflected on this floor by the time you...

00:13:09.050 --> 00:13:09.550
What can it be?

00:13:17.470 --> 00:13:18.410
It's in the ghost.

00:13:18.550 --> 00:13:19.090
See for yourself.

00:13:20.210 --> 00:13:21.450
Leo, she took a bullet.

00:13:21.900 --> 00:13:22.620
Diced it for you.

00:13:22.920 --> 00:13:23.900
I've got a title.

00:13:25.180 --> 00:13:25.980
Captain Baldock.

00:13:27.030 --> 00:13:27.390
And the war.

00:13:29.430 --> 00:13:29.790
And education.

00:13:32.600 --> 00:13:32.960
Well...

00:13:35.060 --> 00:13:35.940
What happened here?

00:13:36.490 --> 00:13:38.750
Since your father died, we've had no repairs.

00:13:40.170 --> 00:13:40.970
I'll remedy that.

00:13:41.330 --> 00:13:43.170
You were my father's tenants, now you're mine.

00:13:44.990 --> 00:13:48.270
Ross, you've got enough to think of with ruined home and barren land.

00:13:48.860 --> 00:13:49.920
I have hands, do I not?

00:13:50.220 --> 00:13:50.980
A spade?

00:13:51.080 --> 00:13:51.500
A plough?

00:13:51.600 --> 00:13:52.400
Well, we can help you.

00:13:54.160 --> 00:13:54.740
Cannot pay.

00:13:54.940 --> 00:13:56.210
I would not expect it.

00:13:56.680 --> 00:13:58.920
You labor long enough for my uncle's mine for a pittance.

00:13:59.000 --> 00:13:59.960
I'll not have you serve me for nothing.

00:14:00.890 --> 00:14:03.190
Ross, what did happen there?

00:14:03.570 --> 00:14:06.380
I grew up.

00:14:08.230 --> 00:14:24.400
Your father left very little of value.

00:14:26.800 --> 00:14:29.380
The house, two derelict mines.

00:14:30.160 --> 00:14:32.080
A few decaying cottages.

00:14:32.940 --> 00:14:36.130
The land, I fear, has been left to rot?

00:14:36.620 --> 00:14:37.060
Entirely.

00:14:37.890 --> 00:14:40.480
So, you come to inquire as to credit.

00:14:41.840 --> 00:14:43.680
As your friend, I would back you to the hilt.

00:14:44.420 --> 00:14:47.290
As your banker, I'm obliged to disappoint.

00:14:48.690 --> 00:14:49.950
Your father had debts.

00:14:50.890 --> 00:14:52.290
Your property is mortgaged.

00:14:52.940 --> 00:14:54.500
Your land has no income.

00:14:55.260 --> 00:14:56.260
I'm of poor risk.

00:14:56.570 --> 00:14:57.050
Quite so.

00:14:57.640 --> 00:14:58.460
Then you'd advise me?

00:14:58.480 --> 00:14:59.700
Look to your own devices.

00:15:00.540 --> 00:15:02.320
Seek your fortune as and where you may.

00:15:02.640 --> 00:15:03.960
Beggars cannot be choosers.

00:15:04.280 --> 00:15:07.490
I hope you may rely on the friend, if not the banker.

00:15:07.750 --> 00:15:11.250
I hope so too, for I need all the friends I can get.

00:15:27.020 --> 00:15:28.740
Plus, Poldark is alive.

00:15:29.680 --> 00:15:29.920
Oh.

00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:33.200
At school, I rather admired him.

00:15:34.270 --> 00:15:35.850
He said what he thought, did what he liked.

00:15:36.520 --> 00:15:37.560
Where did it get him?

00:15:38.130 --> 00:15:39.010
It got him a following.

00:15:40.300 --> 00:15:42.400
It's something we frequently fail to acquire.

00:15:43.460 --> 00:15:45.340
I wonder if he might not be useful to us.

00:15:46.710 --> 00:15:49.070
His father's dead. He's no obvious source of income.

00:15:51.370 --> 00:15:53.410
If we could rally him to our cause...

00:15:53.410 --> 00:15:54.370
To what end?

00:15:54.890 --> 00:15:56.250
He has an ancient family name.

00:15:56.370 --> 00:15:59.140
Doors which are closed to us might open for him.

00:16:01.370 --> 00:16:02.790
What inducements could we offer?

00:16:04.830 --> 00:16:09.380
I find people are very friendly when they cannot afford not to be.

00:16:19.090 --> 00:16:21.620
Elizabeth, where are you going?

00:16:22.660 --> 00:16:23.800
I must speak with Rossman.

00:16:24.120 --> 00:16:24.820
To what purpose?

00:16:27.160 --> 00:16:29.910
To explain, to ask him, what shall we do?

00:16:30.030 --> 00:16:31.130
There is nothing to do.

00:16:31.310 --> 00:16:32.890
You are engaged to Francis.

00:16:34.200 --> 00:16:35.280
But Ross and I-

00:16:35.280 --> 00:16:35.900
Where is he now?

00:16:36.700 --> 00:16:37.580
Has he come to see you?

00:16:37.820 --> 00:16:41.180
What can he offer you but poverty, uncertainty,

00:16:41.440 --> 00:16:42.520
a dubious reputation?

00:16:42.640 --> 00:16:44.440
I do not care about reputation.

00:16:44.600 --> 00:16:45.480
But you should.

00:16:46.850 --> 00:16:47.970
Francis adores you.

00:16:48.490 --> 00:16:50.030
You will be mistress of Trenwith.

00:16:50.430 --> 00:16:53.780
Had Ross not returned, would you have the slightest hesitation?

00:16:53.920 --> 00:16:54.920
He has returned.

00:16:54.980 --> 00:16:58.720
If he still cared for you, would he not

00:16:58.720 --> 00:16:59.980
have been at the door by-

00:17:12.640 --> 00:17:21.720
You would have been surprised to hear about Elizabeth.

00:17:23.150 --> 00:17:24.390
I had no option on the go.

00:17:25.960 --> 00:17:27.320
It was strange how it happened.

00:17:28.140 --> 00:17:29.900
One moment she barely noticed, France.

00:17:30.600 --> 00:17:33.040
She notices mine, his house, his estate.

00:17:36.600 --> 00:17:37.480
That wasn't called for.

00:17:44.240 --> 00:17:45.360
Weddings in a fortnight.

00:17:47.120 --> 00:17:47.700
So soon.

00:17:49.010 --> 00:17:50.370
I wish I could help you, my dear.

00:17:51.110 --> 00:17:52.310
I must find my own way out.

00:18:11.290 --> 00:18:14.860
Who are the crew with you and me?

00:18:15.140 --> 00:18:15.360
What?

00:18:55.820 --> 00:18:57.200
Arming prospect, is it not?

00:19:01.790 --> 00:19:02.690
Lifetime with me.

00:19:02.850 --> 00:19:10.900
I cannot promise to be as fascinating as some.

00:19:12.210 --> 00:19:15.360
Or as bold or reckless.

00:19:17.250 --> 00:19:18.870
One thing I can promise you.

00:19:20.980 --> 00:19:24.470
My undying love and gratitude.

00:19:28.510 --> 00:19:29.490
But if there is a...

00:19:32.010 --> 00:19:33.150
Something that still troubles you.

00:19:35.080 --> 00:19:36.500
There's something that you wish to tell me.

00:19:44.650 --> 00:19:45.050
There is.

00:19:45.190 --> 00:19:55.290
I wish to tell you that I cannot wait to be your wife.

00:20:17.530 --> 00:20:18.430
Should you be doing this?

00:20:18.570 --> 00:20:20.640
I cannot afford a farmhouse.

00:20:20.700 --> 00:20:22.380
Your father would not have wished you to stoop.

00:20:22.540 --> 00:20:24.320
My father would not have wished me to starve.

00:20:26.360 --> 00:20:27.580
She's proved a poor legacy.

00:20:28.600 --> 00:20:29.620
Certainly a fickle one.

00:20:30.760 --> 00:20:31.760
By her time may come again.

00:20:34.840 --> 00:20:35.880
Perhaps I should examine her.

00:20:38.720 --> 00:20:39.560
Is that wise?

00:20:45.360 --> 00:20:46.600
How deep did they drive it?

00:20:47.090 --> 00:20:47.870
30 fathoms.

00:20:48.380 --> 00:20:49.980
Most of it will be underwater by now.

00:20:55.280 --> 00:20:57.420
Ross, my father's concerned.

00:21:00.030 --> 00:21:02.780
But you should make the right choices.

00:21:06.090 --> 00:21:08.840
Face certain realities.

00:21:11.980 --> 00:21:13.780
Accept that your future may lie elsewhere.

00:21:14.040 --> 00:21:15.740
I thank him for his concern.

00:21:18.230 --> 00:21:20.270
Ross, you do know I'm to be married next week.

00:21:22.040 --> 00:21:22.360
And?

00:21:24.650 --> 00:21:26.490
You've not yet accepted our invitation.

00:21:28.500 --> 00:21:29.560
Things to attend to.

00:21:30.000 --> 00:21:30.900
But you must come.

00:21:31.020 --> 00:21:32.240
I'm not one for ceremonies.

00:21:33.190 --> 00:21:34.630
Ross, it is our dearest wish.

00:21:44.710 --> 00:21:48.260
Ross, you must understand.

00:21:49.050 --> 00:21:52.870
When I first met Elizabeth, there was no thought of my coming between you.

00:21:53.270 --> 00:21:54.150
But what could I do?

00:21:55.980 --> 00:21:58.520
My feelings, our feelings, or each other.

00:21:58.540 --> 00:21:59.960
For God's sake, Ross, you rubbed my nose and...

00:22:00.060 --> 00:22:00.500
Let's go!

00:22:31.790 --> 00:22:34.150
For a moment I thought, I thought you'd let me drown.

00:22:34.370 --> 00:22:38.320
For a moment I thought so too.

00:22:46.980 --> 00:22:52.460
Elizabeth, wilt thou hast this man as your wedded husband?

00:22:54.300 --> 00:22:57.820
To live together after God's ordinance in a state of holy matrimony?

00:23:00.540 --> 00:23:12.940
Will thou love, honour and keep, forsake all others, so long as thou shalt be with you?

00:23:15.650 --> 00:23:17.920
I will.

00:23:20.340 --> 00:23:25.940
Those who Lord have joined together, let no man but a son.

00:23:27.730 --> 00:23:28.470
Watch out, turn!

00:23:38.860 --> 00:23:40.160
George has done well for himself.

00:23:41.480 --> 00:23:44.320
As you'll discover, the Warlegans are on the rise.

00:23:44.500 --> 00:23:50.690
Ladies and gentlemen, this is a proud day for the Poldarks.

00:24:16.350 --> 00:24:18.230
So I should have purchased her for you, nephew.

00:24:18.410 --> 00:24:20.310
I broke her my own business these days.

00:24:21.380 --> 00:24:22.480
Well, she'll be wasted here.

00:24:23.320 --> 00:24:25.660
These Poldarks have nothing beyond the name.

00:24:26.980 --> 00:24:29.000
Mine on its knees, mortgage to the hilt.

00:24:29.140 --> 00:24:29.860
We're at Egan's Bank.

00:24:30.320 --> 00:24:32.580
may send in the bailiff's house and when it chooses.

00:24:32.860 --> 00:24:34.400
This is elegant talk for a wedding, Uncle.

00:24:36.460 --> 00:24:39.200
Talk of a prophet is always elegant, George.

00:24:56.860 --> 00:24:58.080
My compliments on the scratch.

00:24:59.070 --> 00:24:59.970
Has he gotten any actual-

00:25:00.000 --> 00:25:02.200
Fighting or another gambling brawl?

00:25:03.010 --> 00:25:04.270
Old habits die hard.

00:25:08.550 --> 00:25:11.850
Cornwall is changing. These are difficult times.

00:25:13.380 --> 00:25:15.920
I trust you will feel you can rely on your friends.

00:25:18.910 --> 00:25:19.350
What for?

00:25:19.980 --> 00:25:21.120
Whatever you might require.

00:25:25.000 --> 00:25:26.460
Thank you, George. I believe I can manage.

00:25:31.180 --> 00:25:34.080
Do you believe breeding can ever be bought?

00:25:34.360 --> 00:25:35.400
You should ask your uncle.

00:25:39.870 --> 00:25:43.230
Elizabeth would be delighted by talk of bailiffs on her wedding day.

00:25:44.020 --> 00:25:46.300
Elizabeth's delight is surely no longer your concern.

00:25:47.210 --> 00:25:49.230
There you are, Ross. I've been sent to find you.

00:26:04.280 --> 00:26:06.280
You see? He had left after all.

00:26:13.740 --> 00:26:14.960
I was glad to see you at church.

00:26:16.750 --> 00:26:18.110
You must wonder why I wished you there.

00:26:25.430 --> 00:26:28.710
After that night, when we had no chance to speak.

00:26:30.540 --> 00:26:31.680
I thought you would come to see me.

00:26:34.980 --> 00:26:35.780
Why would any of that?

00:26:38.100 --> 00:26:40.700
A chance to explain, to apologize.

00:26:40.960 --> 00:26:41.340
For what?

00:26:43.420 --> 00:26:45.180
There was no formal undertaking between us.

00:26:46.730 --> 00:26:47.690
Not officially, no.

00:26:51.470 --> 00:26:52.330
No, there was something.

00:26:54.100 --> 00:26:54.840
An understanding.

00:26:58.420 --> 00:26:59.840
Three years is a long time.

00:27:01.140 --> 00:27:05.020
Elizabeth, remember your duty as a bride is to all your guests.

00:27:05.750 --> 00:27:07.470
I've no taste for fighting, my mom.

00:27:08.710 --> 00:27:10.170
Are you a fan of the sport, Ross?

00:27:10.310 --> 00:27:12.550
Perhaps you'll instruct me in its finer points.

00:27:12.870 --> 00:27:14.830
My dad, if there are any subtleties of combat

00:27:14.830 --> 00:27:16.410
I wish I can offer you advice, ma'am.

